WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.660
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.660
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.730
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.730
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.900
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.900
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.860
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.860
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.870
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.870
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
Keep your eyes on me, okay!?

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:35.610
My name is Kurata Sana, first year junior high school student.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.280
Manager Rei-kun.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.120
The American, Brad, who looks just like an old friend of mine.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.120
The amazing white bat, Babbit!

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:49.130
My best partner in New York, Naozumi-kun.

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:54.090
This...

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.590
...type of thing...

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.100
Who would do such a thing?

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.890
This makes it pretty clear, Sana-chan.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:09.270
Someone has their eye on us.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.560
"Go back to Japan!"

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.490
You Also Have Emerald Eyes

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.440
Is there a goddess of love now?

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.490
This is terrible! How could this happen?

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.080
My room is the same.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.080
Right now I have the 'angry but can't express myself' feeling.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.790
Why do we have to have this 'angry but can't express myself' feeling?

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:37.050
Who would do such an 'angry but can't express myself' thing?

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.930
Do you know, Shimura-san?

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:40.340
My name is Ramsy.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.680
Eh? That face looks like it knows something.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.390
No! I don't know anything.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.190
New York is sure full of puzzles.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.190
Anyway, you won't be able to use this room as it is.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.070
Please get another room ready immediately.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:56.070
- Right.
- Hey, wait!

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.280
Mr. Makubanban!

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.660
That's Makubokyoban...

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:07.500
Looks like that Ramsy-san and Maku-whatever are running away.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.830
I think you forgot to turn off the shower.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:16.090
It feels like we can't trust anyone.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.800
It feels like...

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.880
It feels like I'm getting angry.
I want to find...!

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:21.550
Find what?

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.100
That ghostly girl in the white dress!

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.390
If she doesn't come out,
I'm going to find her myself!

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:27.560
Did she do something?

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.690
I have no idea!
But there might be a clue!

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:33.350
Isn't there a saying that one who's drowning will even eat straw?

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.560
I've never heard that one...

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.280
That should have been 'one who's drowning will grasp at straws'.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.190
Meaning...

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:42.200
Even if we start with just a tiny clue...

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.200
When did you bring that?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.580
If we investigate closely enough, the culprit will reveal himself,

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.870
don't you think, Washington-kun?

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:48.870
Watson.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.750
Ghost in a white dress!

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.080
I am Kurata Sana, 12 years old.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.170
I won't run and I won't hide!

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:00.380
Hiding and doing sneaky things,
you should be ashamed of yourself!

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.430
Sana, could you tone it down a little?

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:08.260
Sana, I can't understand what you're saying...

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.690
Kurata Sana, what kind of behavior is that?

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:17.440
Where where...
where is the Ghostly Girl?

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.780
What is all this noise about?

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.440
Michelle!

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:24.360
What time do you think it is, making such a racket? Have you no manners?

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.570
But it can't be helped, ma'am.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:30.160
A tooth for a tooth. Extreme situations call for extreme methods.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.880
That's a rather cold look.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.960
Our rooms were broken into.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:39.880
I heard.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.760
Isn't Ramsy already preparing other rooms for you?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.380
Moving into them should take care of the problem.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.260
It's not just the rooms.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.100
Yeah! I mean, yes.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.560
Many things have been happening since we've been here.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.060
And the only clue we have is this ghostly girl in a white dress.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.900
Are you referring to me?

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.580
Sicil, you...

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.960
Mama, could you introduce us?

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.880
What, 'Mama'?

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.760
My daughter, Sicil.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.880
I'm Sicil Hamilton.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.890
Pleased to meet you, Naozumi.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.600
Uh, pleased to meet you, too.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.470
Pleased to meet you, uh...

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.390
- Sona...
- Not Sona!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.070
It wasn't me.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:46.200
The person who trashed your rooms wasn't me.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:50.370
How could I do such a thing to important guests?

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.990
Right, Mama?

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:56.000
But, but, someone must have done it, that's a fact.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.960
Because our rooms are a total mess.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:02.880
I've been longing to meet Naozumi. I've always been his fan.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:03.880
Uh, thank you.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.880
Hey, wait! Are you listening to me?

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.680
I've only been able to see pictures of you, I'm so glad to finally meet you.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.600
I'm glad, too.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.890
The color of Naozumi's eyes are the same as mine.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:21.900
Naozumi, Sana, don't you have any sense of being professional actors?

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:26.280
Don't you have an early morning meeting with the stage manager tomorrow?

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.570
And a rehearsal after? Why are you still running around this late at night?

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.160
Hurry and go to your new rooms.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.280
Sicil, you too.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:34.370
Mama...

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.000
Come with me.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:46.300
This week's Sicil-chan.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:58.980
Sicil-chan

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.590
What's this?

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:51.180
Mama! Mama, give it back!

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:53.260
Don't tell me you like her!

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.680
Nah, it's nothing like that...

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.890
Could you be a boy...?

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.690
Don't you know?

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.190
Why did you disobey me, Sicil?

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:05.690
Didn't I say that before formally introducing you that you mustn't meet?

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:11.280
But Mama, you keep saying that but you were never going to let me meet him.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:15.080
Meeting them isn't good for you.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:19.080
What's going on? What do you mean?

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.670
Is it because I can't dance?

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.380
That's not it!

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:31.180
Then... why?

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:35.260
That's not it, Sicil.
It's all for your own good.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.390
I don't understand, Mama.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:41.350
Sicil, please, do as I tell you...

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:45.650
until Dad comes back, okay?

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.450
I'm happy too.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.960
The same color eyes...

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:09.260
Sicil-chan

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.210
Eyes aren't the same color.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.390
Brad, Brad!

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:16.180
Hey, Sicil, good morning!

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.680
Brad! Listen, listen!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.390
You're in a good mood!

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.560
I met Naozumi!

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:25.900
And talked to him, and shook his hand!

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:26.770
Isn't that great?

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:31.690
Ever since the first time I saw his picture in Daddy's room, I thought he was very handsome.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:37.280
I took a photograph from Daddy's files, don't tell anyone, Brad!

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.870
Naozumi's eyes are blue too, just like mine.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:43.290
Who would have thought?
This is so great!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.380
Sicil...

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:53.880
Oh! Japanese Babbit has fallen in love!

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:58.600
American Babbit will make the introductions for now.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:02.890
Pleased to meet everyone. I am the current stage manager, Scott.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:09.860
Full name is Scott Scott. So you can call me by first or last name.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.530
The title of this production is 'Endless Summer',

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:16.860
and is a musical comedy inspired by Shakespeare's 'A Midsummer Night's Dream'.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.870
This is the beginning, Naozumi-kun!

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.160
Yeah!

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.370
The female lead Alice will be played by Sharon Ryan.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.910
The male lead Peter will be played by Harrison Hanks.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:30.670
Tom by Charlie Murphy, Wendy by Sandra Foster, Jimmy by Jodie Hall.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:33.590
And then Sana Kurata and Naozumi Kamura.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:34.380
Yes, sir!
Yes, sir!

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.380
You don't have to stand up.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.340
Yes, sir!

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:40.550
You two will play the twin fairies who try to bring the two leads together

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:42.770
and make them fall in love.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.270
Twin fairies!

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.890
Twins!

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:48.900
There might not be many lines, but they're important roles.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:53.280
I hope you can play this well, but don't break the stage.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.190
What...

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:58.490
Sounds like the stage manager doesn't like us either.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:02.280
There's a proverb that says young labor is worth buying.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:04.580
No matter what it is for...

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.580
Please go home, old man.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.080
Alright, let's begin.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:09.960
Right!

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.670
Sana, Naozumi.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:12.880
Yes!

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.960
You two...

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.100
We ended up running a hundred laps on the roof.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.560
Pushups too. Why?

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:28.060
There's a proverb that says young labor is worth buying.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.270
No matter what it is for...

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.440
Please go home, old man.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.860
Too exhausting!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.860
I wonder if we'll have to keep doing this.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.070
This isn't dance practice!

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:47.870
But Michelle-san said we're way behind the other performers.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:51.880
Maybe this is dancing that requires stamina...

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.800
Hey. Staggering around like this, you must be tired.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.260
Brad? Actually this is
the stagger-dance lesson.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.760
Don't over-do it.

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.390
Sounds like you were very busy last night.

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.600
News travels fast. That's right.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:10.270
Do you know who the culprit might be?

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:13.690
I've told you already, there are all kinds of people here.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:18.190
If a role is snatched away, you don't know what they might do.

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:23.870
It's best if you treat everyone around you as your enemy.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:28.290
You too? Do you hate us too?

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:33.040
I have no reason for hating you.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.460
That's true.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:40.670
Don't be mad, Brad.
I know you're a good person.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:45.890
It's your own fault. You're the one who said to treat everyone around us as enemies.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.470
Aaah! Kurata Sana!

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:50.270
A lot of things will happen here.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:57.190
A big fat biscuit, line, line, triangle, heart plus wings and you get Babbit!

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:00.490
Aaah! Kurata Sana!

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:03.200
A lot of things will happen here.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.700
Let's have some lunch, Naozumi-kun.
If we don't eat we'll have no energy.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:07.950
That's true.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.790
Naozumi-kun! Are you alright?

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.460
Odd!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.590
Rest here a little more,
I'll go buy some food.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:17.880
I'm sorry.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.170
I'll be right back!

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:20.090
Okay.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:24.890
You need more energy...

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.680
I'm useless...

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.730
You must be Naozumi Kamura.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:40.280
I know your secret.

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:45.950
Do you know the real reason you were invited to New York?

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:50.910
What? The real reason?

00:12:50.910 --> 00:13:01.050
{parte b}

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:04.090
Babbit
counting
song

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:07.180
One, two, one-two-three-one...

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:10.100
One pile, one pile, there's one pile oh...

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.850
The one and only Babbit family clan, no problem...

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:16.020
One pile, one pile, there's one pile oh...

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:18.810
The one and only Babbit family clan, no problem...

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:22.110
One, two, one-two-three-two...

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.950
I want to confide in someone but I can't.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:27.780
The hardest part is when I'm trying to be serious.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.950
I want to confide in someone but I can't.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.790
The hardest part is when I'm trying to be serious.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:37.120
One, two, one-two-three-three...

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:39.880
Sri Lanka is next to India.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.800
It's famous for its red tea.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:45.920
Sri Lanka is next to India.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:48.800
It's famous for its red tea.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.890
Wahahaha! To be continued!

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.890
Each verse begins with words that rhyme with one/two/three; e.g. three rhymes with 'Sri' from 'Sri Lanka'

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:55.390
Who are you?

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:59.980
Didn't I tell you? I'm someone who knows your secret.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.650
What does that mean?

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:06.530
You want to know, don't you? The real reason you were asked to New York City.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.320
The real reason?

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.950
Yeah. You are...

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:13.620
Naozumi-kun! Naozumi-kun!

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:16.460
They sell some strange stuff these days!

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:17.750
It's called Udon burger!

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.540
Try some Japanese food and get back some of your energy!

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.340
Naozumi, I'll be back.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:30.930
I found a strange store! They also sell Matsu dog and tempura sandwich or something!

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.720
Let's try those out next time!

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:40.060
He was referring to me specifically, not the both of us.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:47.240
So the reason really is just me. All that's happened since we arrived was because of me.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.650
What's wrong, Naozumi-kun?

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:49.530
Uh, nothing.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.370
Try some Udon burger!

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:55.240
It doesn't taste too bad...

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:57.660
Must be bad.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:02.040
Please be careful of American 'Japanese' food.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:05.960
This week's Sana-chan.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:12.470
Boy... what a big mistake. It would've been better not to eat it.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:16.140
I'm sorry, Naozumi-kun.
Will you be okay this afternoon?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.140
Naozumi-kun?

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.350
Are you alright?
You're spacing out.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:25.270
I'm fine! I'm fine! Like the Cantonese say, 'Mo Mun Tai'(No problem)!

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:27.650
Are you sure? Don't over-do it...

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:30.450
Really, I'm fine.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.580
Go back to Japan.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.450
Or else...

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.170
Second warning.

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:43.460
Next time it'll be the real thing.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:45.150
You want to know, don't you? The real reason you were asked to New York City.

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:50.900
If their real target is just me...

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:56.530
...then I've just pulled Sana into a dangerous situation.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:57.910
It's me...

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:03.460
Who? Who's looking at us as a problem?

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:12.260
Michelle-san?
Sicil? Brad? Or... or...

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.760
Looks like they were very frightened.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.770
They'll be gone with their tails between their legs very soon.

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:25.940
They thought these knives were real.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:28.440
This should do it.

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:35.150
Fly!

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:37.360
Oh! We forgot Rei-kun!

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:42.370
I've met him! Gary Hamilton. The big movie producer!

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:48.040
I'm really really moved! Great!

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:51.550
His face looked like this,
with lots of character.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:54.670
But with no sunglasses,
that's just my trademark.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:57.470
Mr. Hamilton told me...

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:01.760
"I've been watching their talent for a long time.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:05.020
And I'm looking forward to seeing "Mizumi no Kata" soon.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:09.440
They will definitely be a sensation in this production.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:13.110
Mr. Sagami, you better damn well believe me."

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:17.610
Uh, he didn't say "damn well", that was just me too. He's just so full of charm.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:21.030
Wow, I want to become a producer as cool as he is.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:22.370
That's probably not possible.

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:28.330
Mr. Hamilton says he'll be back next week, so do your best! Sana-chan, Naozumi-kun!

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.750
Eh?

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:35.210
What's up with you two?
You look deflated.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.550
Want a look at this?

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:42.720
Oh! This is Kodocha Episode 69! This hasn't been aired has it? Can I really see it?

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:45.350
The performer has become the fan! What's up with that?

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:49.350
Go back to Japan. Or else...

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:51.860
What the hell is going on?!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:55.030
That something like this should happen while I'm gone!

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.230
Let's go home.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.030
Let's go back to Japan.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:00.660
What?

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:09.540
I just wanted to try my abilities on Broadway.

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:18.470
Although quitting is regrettable, it's not worth risking my life for.

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:20.130
Naozumi-kun...

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:25.930
I don't want to place you in anymore danger.

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:32.560
This is a problem. To keep one's life is definitely important...

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:37.570
...but to give up on such a big job so easily...

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:40.450
...but you can't replace a lost life...

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:41.860
...but...

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:45.580
Of course life is important.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:50.750
But... I don't want to do that.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:52.250
Sana-chan.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:56.170
This is mysterious, strange, I don't understand it at all.

00:19:56.170 --> 00:20:00.260
We were invited here by Mr. Gary Hamilton...

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:03.760
...and we're here for a musical production.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:07.350
But having come here, it seems like we've been targeted.

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:10.270
The car suddenly came at us, and the chandelier also fell.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.980
We thought it was that ghostly girl but she's Hamilton's family.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.940
Our rooms were made a total disaster, our tire exploded...

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:16.570
...and Maeda-san is in the hospital,

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.820
The dance classes consisted of running laps.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:23.030
And then... and then... suddenly we're threatened.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:27.870
We can't figure out what is going on, or who is doing all this...

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:35.670
...but those people who are threatening us and trying to make us do as they want...

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:41.130
I just feel that they're low. I hate this, I feel horrible.

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:44.340
That's why... I am not going home.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:48.350
It's not Sicil's fault.

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:05.820
Now what are you up to?

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:10.660
Thank you for your care for the past few days.

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:21.340
I see. Well, this has been short.
I will have the car ready immediately.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:24.760
I wonder if there are seats on the flight.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:30.350
We are not going back to Japan.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:34.730
We will be moving to a hotel for the time being.

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:38.440
And we will be looking into renting a place.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.940
We will do our best on stage.

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:42.650
And will be going to rehearsal every day.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.860
We want the production to be a success, Michelle-san.

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:47.860
It will be a pleasure working with you.

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:49.570
Japanese-style bow.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.960
Why are they doing this?

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:12.470
Naozumi...

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:30.660
